{"chunk_id": "9ca0c825f559", "text": "Amba appeals to the warrior-sage Parashurama (Rama of the Bhrigu line) to avenge the ruin of her life. Bhishma had abducted her from her swayamvara, but released her after learning she loved King Salwa; Salwa then rejected her because Bhishma had taken her first. With her honor and prospects destroyed, Amba declares Bhishma the root of her misery and begs for his death. Parashurama initially hesitates, bound by a vow not to take up arms except for Brahmanas, yet the sage Akritavrana reminds him of his promise to protect those who seek refuge and to challenge the mightiest Kshatriya. Parashurama confronts Bhishma and commands him to marry Amba, but Bhishma refuses on grounds of vow and duty. Their dispute escalates into fierce mutual taunts, culminating in an agreement to meet in single combat at Kurukshetra.\nAmba urges Parashurama to kill Bhishma; bound by vows, Parashurama confronts Bhishma, whose refusal leads both to agree to fight at Kurukshetra.\nThemes: vengeance, dharma and duty, vows and honor, teacher\u2013disciple conflict, female grievance", "vector": [-0.0029227002523839474, -0.03438470885157585, -0.01676085963845253, 0.014090987853705883, -0.028937092050909996, 0.019592540338635445, -0.020536435768008232, -0.0038429966662079096, -0.022221960127353668, -0.02524241991341114, 0.011535732075572014, 0.0007230901974253356, 0.03020460531115532, -0.0005617011920548975, -0.0007643855060450733, 0.0040115490555763245, 0.052911996841430664, 0.00928387138992548, 0.01196722686290741, -0.013996598310768604, -0.004021662287414074, -0.004038517829030752, 0.0025687399320304394, 0.03157999366521835, -0.034195929765701294, 0.022720875218510628, 0.020846571773290634, -0.021561235189437866, -0.0009969879174605012, -0.02799319662153721, -0.010416544042527676, -0.009081607684493065, -0.013956146314740181, -0.014347188174724579, -0.03659611567854881, 0.007780382875353098, -0.008306266739964485, -0.015034882351756096, 0.02022629790008068, 0